	"notes": "Linear's homepage is almost all dark background, white text, and one big picture of its own app sitting front and centre. On a laptop that picture and the headline above it stretch nearly the full width of the window; on a bigger screen they stop growing and hold at about 1300 pixels wide, with more black space appearing on both sides instead. On a phone the picture does not get chopped off at the edges — it shrinks all the way down so the whole app screenshot still fits, and the menu bar turns into a stacked list rather than a row of links. Further down the page, more screenshots of the product repeat the exact same centred, capped-width trick as the hero.",
